@page "/privacy"
@using ComicPlatform.Components.Shared

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Catkoom</PageTitle>

<LegalPage Title="Privacy Policy" Updated="October 17, 2026">
    <p>
        This policy explains what information Catkoom collects, why we collect it, who can see it, and the choices
        you have. It applies to the Catkoom website.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Information you give us</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address, username and password. Passwords are stored in a protected, hashed form, not as readable text.</li>
        <li><strong>Date of birth:</strong> collected when you sign up or when we ask you for it (see section 3).</li>
        <li><strong>Profile details you choose to add:</strong> a profile picture, bio, and links to your social accounts or website.</li>
        <li><strong>Content you post:</strong> series, chapters, cover images, creator posts, comments and replies, and the likes and follows you make.</li>
        <li><strong>Reports you file:</strong> the category and the written reason you give.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment setup for creators:</strong> if you connect a Stripe account to receive earnings, Stripe collects and holds your payment and identity details. We only keep the account reference and whether setup is complete.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Information from other services</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>If you sign in with Google or Facebook, we receive your email address, name and account identifier from them. We don't receive your password.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Information collected automatically</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>How many times chapters are viewed. To count one view per person per chapter per day, we keep a short-lived record of which account (or visitor cookie) opened which chapter that day. It's deleted within about a day and isn't used to build a history of what you read.</li>
        <li>Cookies and similar storage that keep you signed in and remember your settings (see section 6).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To run your account, sign you in, and show your subscriptions, follows and comments.</li>
        <li>To send emails you need, such as confirming your email address and resetting your password.</li>
        <li>To show you content that's appropriate for your age.</li>
        <li>To keep the site safe: handling reports, removing content, and dealing with accounts that break our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.</li>
        <li>To make the site work and improve it, for example by counting views for rankings.</li>
        <li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Your date of birth</h2>
    <p>
        We use your date of birth only to check that you're old enough to have an account and to decide which
        age-rated series (13+, 16+ or 18+) you can see. It is never shown on your profile or to other users.
        Once saved, it can't be changed from your account page, so please enter it correctly.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who can see your information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Public on Catkoom:</strong> your username, profile picture, bio, social links, your series and creator posts, and your comments and replies.</li>
        <li><strong>Not public:</strong> your email address, date of birth, password and reports you file. Our moderators can see reports and the information needed to act on them.</li>
        <li><strong>Co-authors:</strong> if you add someone as a co-author, they can see and edit that series.</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>Services that help us run Catkoom</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Email delivery: [email provider, currently a Google (Gmail) account for testing] sends the confirmation and password-reset emails.</li>
        <li>Sign-in: Google and Facebook, if you choose to use them.</li>
        <li>Payments: Stripe, for creator payouts.</li>
        <li>Hosting and storage: [hosting provider to be added] stores our database and uploaded images.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        These providers only get the information they need to do their job. We don't sell your personal
        information. We may share information when the law requires it or to protect people's safety.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
        We keep your information while your account is open. When you delete your account, we remove your personal
        data, though some information may stay for a limited time in backups, or longer if we're required to keep
        it by law or to deal with a report or dispute.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Cookies and similar storage</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sign-in cookie:</strong> keeps you logged in, and is needed for the site to work.</li>
        <li><strong>Security cookies:</strong> protect forms against forgery.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitor cookie:</strong> a random ID, used for logged-out readers so that opening the same chapter several times in a day counts as one view. It isn't linked to an account.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings:</strong> your light or dark theme choice is saved in your browser.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't use these to track you across other websites.</p>

    <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You can edit your profile details at any time in your account settings.</li>
        <li>You can download or delete your personal data from <strong>Account &rarr; Personal data</strong>.</li>
        <li>You can ask us to correct information that is wrong, or to explain what we hold about you, by contacting us below.</li>
        <li>[Add any rights that apply under the privacy law you operate under, for example the Data Privacy Act of 2012 in the Philippines, after legal review.]</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>
        Catkoom isn't for children under 13. If we find out we've collected information from someone under 13, we
        will delete the account and the information.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
        We protect your information with measures such as hashed passwords and encrypted connections. No system is
        completely secure, so please use a strong, unique password.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this policy. When we make an important change, we'll tell you on the site or by email, and we'll
        update the date at the top.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests about your information: [contact email].</p>
</LegalPage>
